I implemented the node itself but left out both operations additions.

- **Log file:** the target is `wasm32-unknown-unknown` with no WASI adapter, and the world has no filesystem interface, so the component can't write `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log`.
- **Metadata fetch:** the node's declared capability is only `inference-llm`. Fetching would need an `http-client` import, which this node isn't granted. It would also send input text to an external service.

If you want either, the graph needs to grant the node that capability (for example a scoped `http-client` or a log sink). Then the world can be extended.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{selection, run-info, digest};

    import aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0;

    export run: func(selected: selection, info: run-info) -> digest;
}
```

